// =============================
// ========== OVERRUN ==========
// ======== OVERLOADED =========
// ==== ADVANCED - ENDURANCE ===
// ==== MADE BY PLUZORMINUZ ====
// =============================

// =============================
// ===== IMPORTANT RELAYS ======
// =============================

// wave_start_relay					start the wave with bomb(s) that never resets
// wave_start_relay_ironman			start the wave with bomb(s) that resets at 55s

// wave_finished_relay				clear the nav brushes, revert hologram to empty, DOES NOT HELP YOU TO SELECT A NEW BOMB PATH
// wave_finished_relay_final		unleash the error

// =============================
// ======== PATH SELECT ========
// =============================
// path_mode_select					used in InitWaveOutput to choose the bomb paths,
//										Action = SetValue
//										Param is a number from 1-44 in quotations
//										example:
//														InitWaveOutput
//														{
//															Target path_mode_select
//															Action SetValue
//															Param "28"
//														}								
//									this is used to set up how the bombs and tanks will path through the map
//									for example, if you want the wave to feature 2 bombs and 1 tank, then look in the TYPE column
//									for "2B1T". the type offers 3 combinations of 2 bombs 1 tank, under mode 8-10
//									so you can pick, for instance, mode 9 for the 2 bombs to go together, and that the tank go through the other route.
//									the keywords b1, b2, b3, b4, t1, t2, f1 are tags you can use on bots to make them prefer specific routes
//									for tanks, tanks starting from "tank1" will follow path "t1" and "tank2" follow "t2"
//									if you pick the same mode again (between map resets), the remaining combinations will be
//									picked at random until all cases have been picked, then the mode is shuffled.
//
//									if this relay is fired mid-wave, the hologram for the new route will flash for 40 seconds before disappearing
//									*** THIS DOES NOT PAUSE BOTS FROM SPAWNING
//									reference table here https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1rjCcpBRZR5p9ftUoZoi0t28ddedKZJ3mRtniuIXdq-g/edit#gid=1293768176
//
//									if you want to trigger a mid-wave break AND change route, make the Param number negative.
//									so "-32" for example, sets up 4 bombs and 1 tank all on the same path, together with a 40 second wave break
//									*** THIS WILL PAUSE BOTS SPAWN AND STUN BOTS
//
//									selecting from the path mode will automatically enable the correct bombs
//									however, during a wave, the number of active bombs will not decrease automatically
//									if you wish to decrease the number of bombs during a wave, try to do so *during* a wave break and use dummy wave to disable them
//									see below for bomb names.

// =============================
// ======= MID WAVE BREAK ======
// =============================
// upgradestation_forward_40		opens the forward upgrade station for 40 seconds only. does not pause bots spawn

// =============================
// ======== INTEL NAMES ========
// =============================
// intel1
// intel2
// intel3
// intel4

// =============================
// ====== BOT SPAWN NAMES ======
// =============================
// spawnbot						spawns from any gate. added for compatibility from other missions
// spawnbot_carrier				spawns from any gate
// spawnbot_carrier_gate#		spawns from specific gate of the carrier, 1-6 going clockwise from the left gate closest to the exit
// spawnbot_mission_sniper		spawns from gates 1,3,4,6
// spawnbot_mission_spy			spawns from gates 1,3,4,6
// spawnbot_mission_buster		spawns from gates 2,5
// spawnbot_carrier_giant		spawns from gates 2,5
// spawnbot_carrier_left		spawns from the left gates (1-3)
// spawnbot_carrier_right		spawns from the right gates (4-6)

// ==== the above spawns are all inside the carrier
// spawnbot_road				spawns behind the booth to the left of the carrier
//
// =============================
// ===== TANK SPAWN NAMES ======
// =============================
// tank1		follows tank path T1
// tank2		follows tank path T2
// tank3		follows tank path T1
// tank4		follows tank path T2
// ==== note: you can spawn all 4 tanks at once without overlapping
// ==== note: due to the logic setup and the hologram, you can NOT specify which path (upper/lower) the tank will take
//            it will be determined by the tank hologram randomly
//

// =============================
// ======== FLANK NAMES ========
// =============================
// flank_left					flank to the high ground to the left of the first choke at front
// flank_right					flank behind the Dropdown House to the right of the first choke at front

// =============================
// ======== MAP TIMING =========
// =============================
// Tank to Hatch (lower route) -> 136s (2m16s)
// Tank to Hatch (upper route) -> 136s (2m16s)
// Super Scout Spawn to Hatch (lower route) -> 26s
// Super Scout Spawn to Hatch (upper route) -> 28s
// Scout (with bomb) Spawn to Hatch (lower route) -> 55s
// Scout (with bomb) Spawn to Hatch (upper route) -> 59s

// Human Scout to Hatch (upper route)-> 22s
// Human Scout to Hatch (lower route)-> 21s
// Human Pyro to Hatch (upper route)-> 30s
// Human Pyro to Hatch (lower route)-> 28s
// Human Heavy to Hatch (upper route)-> 39s
// Human Heavy to Hatch (lower route)-> 36s

// =============================
// ========= MAP NOTES =========
// =============================
// with shortcuts, a Scout can travel from Robot Spawn back to Hatch in 16 seconds.
// some routes are intended to better utilize jump height

#base robot_giant.pop
#base robot_standard.pop

WaveSchedule
